# S1-M-218 / THM-M-1027: Existence of Wiener process

This Stage1 file records a conservative Lean boundary for the existence of a
Wiener process, also known as standard Brownian motion.  The pinned mathlib
snapshot has Gaussian-process, independent-increment, filtration/adaptedness,
Gaussian-real-law, Ionescu-Tulcea, and Kolmogorov-process infrastructure, but no
terminal theorem constructing a continuous Wiener process was found in the local
dependency closure.

The declarations below therefore normalize the theorem statement around a
nonnegative-real time index.  The proved content is limited to low-risk wrappers
around existing mathlib APIs.  No construction of Brownian motion is claimed in
this file.  An external Lean 4 project, `RemyDegenne/brownian-motion`, contains
the terminal Brownian construction names; this file does not import or pin that
project.
-/

noncomputable section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped ENNReal NNReal

